 :claim "Battery and power management: on battery the level reads correctly through the drain, the machine warns at low, and it sleeps."
 :host {:model "MacBookPro18,4", :cpu "Apple M1 Max", :os "Darwin 25.4.0 arm64"}
 :commit "134146345189990190ee18573f593ba7968b1d72"
 :verdicts
 {"level-reads-through-the-drain" {:green? true, :reason :evidence, :evidence "kernel-serial.log: AIUEOS_BATTERY_OK steps=8 warn-from=10 critical=5 ac=0 band-y=786, with battery-steps.txt holding all eight step lines -- AC at 100, then battery 100/80/60/40/20/10/5, each with its warn-px and base-px"}
  "the-reading-is-checked-against-pixels" {:green? true, :reason :evidence, :evidence "battery-steps.txt: steps 100..20 read the normal POWER colour (warn-px 0, base-px 8..12), step 10 reads warn-px 8 base-px 0, step 5 reads warn-px 9 base-px 0 -- the level is verified against the band's own pixels, not against the variable that produced it. The probe line in kernel-serial.log shows the band itself: band-y=786, at70=00c0c0c0 (the POWER colour), at300=00202830 (the band background)"}
  "the-warning-appears-at-low" {:green? true, :reason :marker, :marker "AIUEOS_BATTERY_OK warn-from=10: the warning colour 0x00d08060 is present exactly when the level is at or below 10 on battery, and absent above it (steps 100/80/60/40/20 all warn-px 0)"}
  "the-machine-sleeps" {:green? true, :reason :evidence, :evidence "suspend-run-serial.log (the browser-desktop-suspend gate's own run, receipts/vm-20261024/suspend): AIUEOS_GUEST_BROWSER_SUSPEND_GO ops=151 hash=0b9dbd72 state=dd700ef5, SUSPEND_ENTER screen=black, SUSPEND_RESUME ops=151 hash=0b9dbd72 state=dd700ef5 frame-intact=1 state-intact=1"}
  "the-sleep-was-real-on-the-host" {:green? true, :reason :evidence, :evidence "suspend-run-receipt.edn (the same gate run's host evidence): before-sha == after-sha (a57e4a52...), during-black? true, resume-ms 51, and its own verdicts guest-browser-suspend / audio / backup all green"}
  "no-failure-path-hit" {:green? true, :reason :marker, :marker "kernel-serial.log carries zero AIUEOS_EVIDENCE_STOP and zero AIUEOS_VIRTIO_GPU_FAIL across all eight steps"}}
 :run
 {:mechanism "The reference VM has no battery device to read -- no ACPI BAT0, and QEMU's PC machines expose none -- so the level is the guest's own state behind AIUEOS_BATTERY_PROBE and the stage walks it. The band is repainted by the stage itself because show() returns before painting it when the damage rectangle is empty (framebuffer.c:790) and this stage's frame does not change between steps."
  :procedure "AIUEOS_GUEST_BROWSER=1 AIUEOS_TEST_NET=1 AIUEOS_BATTERY_PROBE=1 AIUEOS_QEMU_TIMEOUT=6000 ./os/aiueos/scripts/smoke-qemu-uefi.sh via kbb run-task browser-desktop-battery (AIUEOS_LOOP_EXIT_OK=1 so the smoke ends at the desktop loop instead of its 6000s wall clock); the gate prints AIUEOS_COMPOSITOR_GUEST_BROWSER_BATTERY_OK. Sleep evidence: one browser-desktop-suspend run of the same tree family, committed as receipts/vm-20261024/suspend."
  :reading "every step's level is checked against sampled pixels of the POWER field (aiueos_desktop_sample_rgb over the eight glyph cells), never against battery_level itself"}
 :caveats
 ["the power source is synthetic: there is no battery in this machine, so the level is driven by the gate. The reading, the warning and the sleep are real guest behaviour; the discharge is not -- :device evidence (a real cell draining) stays open"
  "the sleep evidence is from a SECOND run (the browser-desktop-suspend gate's own receipt, 2026-10-24), not from the battery serial: the chain stops at backup in every profile run -- AIUEOS_GUEST_BROWSER_BACKUP leftover=no-records sits at line 769 of the I3, pointer-fix and ui-scale serials too -- so audio and suspend never run in the battery profile. The battery judge therefore validates suspend markers only when they appear on its own serial, and this receipt cites the suspend gate's run for that half, as I3's receipt cited two runs"
  "suspend-to-idle is not ACPI S3 (ADR-0273): the RAM stays powered and the lid is a key"]
 :green? true}